{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .litehive/tasks/T-0301-fix-bubblewrap-argv-0-rewrite-and-add-per-engine/task.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: T-0301\nslug: fix-bubblewrap-argv-0-rewrite-and-add-per-engine\ntitle: Fix bubblewrap argv[0] rewrite and add per-engine extra_ro_binds\ndepends_on: []\ntask_type: bugfix\nmodel: null\nmode: implementation\npipeline_mode: full\nstatus: queued\nflag_reason: null\nflag_count: 0\npipeline_status: backlog\npriority: high\npm_complexity: moderate\nplanned_effort: s\ncreated_at: '2026-04-10T10:09:43+00:00'\nupdated_at: '2026-04-10T12:11:28+00:00'\ngoal: The bubblewrap sandbox path in SandboxLauncher._wrap_bubblewrap does not rewrite\n  argv[0] the way _wrap_docker does, so an engine binary that is not on PATH inside\n  the sandbox (e.g. codex installed via nvm at /home/alexey/.nvm/versions/node/v24.13.1/bin/codex)\n  fails at execvp. Additionally there is no mechanism to bind-mount a binary's package/runtime\n  directory (node + codex package under ~/.nvm), so even after fixing argv[0] the\n  Node shebang script cannot launch. Fix both so that codex and claude (both nvm-installed\n  on this host) can actually run inside the bubblewrap sandbox end-to-end. This is\n  the first blocker before we can enable sandbox mode.\nacceptance_criteria:\n- _wrap_bubblewrap rewrites invocation.argv[0] to the resolved absolute host binary\n  path (matching the behavior of _wrap_docker)\n- ExternalEngineSandboxPolicy gains an extra_ro_binds field (list of host paths) that\n  _wrap_bubblewrap adds as --ro-bind entries; engines with runtime dependency directories\n  (codex, claude) declare their required binds via config\n- 'Real spawned subprocess integration test: construct a SandboxLauncher, wrap a codex\n  --version call, actually execute it, assert exit=0 and stdout contains a version\n  string. Same for claude if claude is installed'\n- Similar test for a minimal python3 + uv invocation so the happy path is covered\n  even on hosts without codex\n- Graceful error if an engine's extra_ro_binds paths do not exist on the host (clear\n  message, fail closed)\nconstraints: []\nplan:\n- Update sandbox config model/normalization to support per-engine extra_ro_binds and\n  preserve round-trip formatting/status coverage.\n- Align bubblewrap wrapping with docker by rewriting argv[0] to the resolved absolute\n  host binary path before exec.\n- Extend bubblewrap mount planning to add engine-declared read-only binds and fail\n  closed with a clear SandboxError when any declared bind path is missing.\n- Add focused unit coverage for config normalization/formatting, bubblewrap argv[0]\n  rewriting, extra_ro_binds mount propagation, and missing-bind errors.\n- 'Add real subprocess integration coverage for bubblewrap-wrapped version checks:\n  python3+uv baseline always, codex mandatory on this host, claude conditional when\n  installed.'\nhuman_checkpoints: []\nsubagents: []\ngit:\n  auto_commit: true\n  commit_message: 'litehive: complete T-0301 fix-bubblewrap-argv-0-rewrite-and-add-per-engine'\n  commit_sha: null\n  checkpoint_base_sha: null\n  checkpoint_attempts: 0\n  rolled_back_checkpoint_attempt: null\n  merge_agent_attempts: 0\n  worktree_path: null\nretry_policy:\n  max_retries: null\n  stage_retry_limit: null\ncreated_from: null\nupstream_origin: null\ngithub_origin: null\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
